   expression's derived size; proved in lean_frontend/Core_reduction_lemMeasureProofs.lean. -/

/- FUEL MEASURE (fuel-parameter arc C3, 2026-09-05; Lean-only): the three point-free
   `function` tails, measurable since lem d4ba548 hoists the scrutinee into the head
   as `lemTail`. one_step_unseq_aux recurses on the tail of `lemTail` only.
   get_ctx/get_ctx_unseq_aux share ONE fuel counter: get_ctx descends into ONE child
   (the LEFT operand of Ewseq/Esseq, the body of Ebound/Eannot) or hands the Eunseq
   operand list to the aux, which recurses into get_ctx on the head and into itself
   on the rest — so the measure is the block's CALL DEPTH, not a size:
   `CerbCoreMeasure.getCtxBound` (lean_frontend/CerbCoreMeasure.lean, the
   extra_import at the top of this file; fuel-measure-cost arc, 2026-09-07/08). It
   replaces C3's whole-arena `lemSize g + 1` / `lemSize_aux2 lemTail + 1`, which
   re-sized the ENTIRE arena on every driver step (45 %/39 % of CPU samples on
   csmith 369/371, docs/2026-09-07_fuel-measure-cost-record.md §D2). One unit per
   worker frame, the maximum over the possible children, the is_irreducible pruning
   ignored — so every cross-call strictly decreases the callee's measure and the
   bound is never short. Proved in lean_frontend/Core_reduction_lemMeasureProofs.lean. -/

